<Description>
    <Header>
        <h1 id="contribution-guide" class="cg-toc-anchor">Contribution Guide</h1>
    </Header>
    <Content>
        <p>Thank you for contributing to the <strong>Syncfusion<sup style="font-size:70%">&reg;</sup> Toolkit for Blazor</strong>. Five steps take you from a fork to a pull request. For a larger change, such as a new component or a breaking API change, open an <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/issues" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">issue</a> first so the team can confirm it is in scope.</p>
        <div class="cg-callout">
            By participating you agree to the <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Code of Conduct</a>. To report a security vulnerability, follow <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/SECURITY.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>SECURITY.md</code></a> and do not open a public issue.
        </div>
    </Content>
</Description>

<Description>
    <Header>
        <h2 id="step-1-fork-and-clone" class="cg-toc-anchor">1. Fork and clone the repository</h2>
    </Header>
    <Content>
        <p>Fork <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">syncfusion/blazor-toolkit</a>, then clone your fork. You need the .NET SDK (8.0, 9.0, or 10.0), Node.js 22 with npm, and Git.</p>
        <pre class="cg-codeblock"><code>git clone https://github.com/&lt;your-account&gt;/blazor-toolkit.git
cd blazor-toolkit
npm ci</code></pre>
        <p><strong>Success check:</strong> <code>dotnet --list-sdks</code> lists an SDK that matches a target framework of the project you will edit.</p>
        <p>Before starting, open or claim an issue (for example one labelled <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/issues?q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22good+first+issue%22" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>good first issue</code></a>) so nobody duplicates your work.</p>
    </Content>
</Description>

<Description>
    <Header>
        <h2 id="step-2-create-a-branch" class="cg-toc-anchor">2. Create a focused branch</h2>
    </Header>
    <Content>
        <p>Branch from <code>main</code> using a descriptive prefix: <code>fix/</code>, <code>feat/</code>, <code>docs/</code>, <code>test/</code>, or <code>chore/</code>. Keep one logical change per branch.</p>
        <pre class="cg-codeblock"><code>git checkout -b fix/&lt;short-description&gt; main</code></pre>
        <p><strong>Success check:</strong> <code>git branch --show-current</code> prints your new branch name.</p>
    </Content>
</Description>

<Description>
    <Header>
        <h2 id="step-3-change-and-validate" class="cg-toc-anchor">3. Make and validate the change</h2>
    </Header>
    <Content>
        <p>Follow the .NET Foundation coding style with two project exceptions: omit the <code>private</code> keyword and use hard tabs. Add or update tests; bug fixes need a regression test. Then run the same checks CI runs:</p>
        <pre class="cg-codeblock"><code>dotnet restore src/Syncfusion.Blazor.Toolkit.csproj
dotnet build   src/Syncfusion.Blazor.Toolkit.csproj -c Release --no-restore
dotnet test    tests/Syncfusion.Blazor.Toolkit.BUnitTest/ -c Release
npx playwright test --reporter=line
npm run lint:security
npx gulp security-xss-scan</code></pre>
        <p><strong>Success check:</strong> every command completes without errors. Avoid new NuGet dependencies unless you justify them in the pull request. Do not commit secrets, <code>bin/</code>, <code>obj/</code>, or <code>node_modules/</code>.</p>
        <p>More detail: <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/DEVELOPMENT.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>DEVELOPMENT.md</code></a> and <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>CONTRIBUTING.md</code></a>.</p>
    </Content>
</Description>

<Description>
    <Header>
        <h2 id="step-4-commit" class="cg-toc-anchor">4. Commit using the repository convention</h2>
    </Header>
    <Content>
        <p>Use a Conventional Commits style message and reference the issue you fix.</p>
        <pre class="cg-codeblock"><code>git add -A
git commit -m "fix(SfDialog): prevent focus loss when closing"
git push origin fix/&lt;short-description&gt;</code></pre>
        <p><strong>Success check:</strong> the branch appears on your fork with your commits.</p>
    </Content>
</Description>

<Description>
    <Header>
        <h2 id="step-5-open-a-pull-request" class="cg-toc-anchor">5. Open a pull request</h2>
    </Header>
    <Content>
        <p>Open a pull request targeting <code>main</code> and complete the <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">pull request template</a>.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Include <code>Fixes #&lt;issue&gt;</code> on its own line in the description.</li>
            <li>Attach Before / After screenshots for any visible UI change.</li>
            <li>Tick <strong>Allow edits from maintainers</strong>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Success check:</strong> CI (bUnit on .NET 8, 9 and 10, Playwright, vulnerability scan, ESLint security scan, XSS scan, and pack) passes. At least two team members review the pull request, and a maintainer squash-merges it once approved. You are then listed on the <a href="/contributors">Contributors</a> page.</p>
        <p>Need help? Use <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/discussions" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">GitHub Discussions</a> or <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/SUPPORT.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>SUPPORT.md</code></a>.</p>
    </Content>
</Description>

